  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890244",
      "title": "Bonus: Exploring tsconfig.json",
      "sourceHash": "ce0be656f39e44679c617861a655f9afa2689d88c2beb607cd52b54c827b741c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.24,
          "end": 5.06,
          "en": "Now as a bonus in this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.06,
          "end": 7.835,
          "en": "I wanna have another look at this tsconfig",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.835,
          "end": 9.99,
          "en": "JSON file since I promised that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.99,
          "end": 12.01,
          "en": "and since it is important to at least",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.01,
          "end": 15.41,
          "en": "understand the basics about this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.41,
          "end": 18.7,
          "en": "This is a file which you can add to any project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.7,
          "end": 20.87,
          "en": "where you are using TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.87,
          "end": 23.54,
          "en": "So where you are compiling TypeScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.54,
          "end": 24.81,
          "en": "to JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.81,
          "end": 28.8,
          "en": "And then this will configure this compilation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.8,
          "end": 30.76,
          "en": "Now speaking of the compilation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.76,
          "end": 33.76,
          "en": "in this reactant TypeScript project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.76,
          "end": 36.83,
          "en": "the compiler is invoked automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.83,
          "end": 39,
          "en": "when we start the development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39,
          "end": 42.27,
          "en": "or when we built this project for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.27,
          "end": 46.33,
          "en": "We are using a behind the scenes, build workflow setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.33,
          "end": 49.633,
          "en": "where this TypeScript compiler is integrated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.79,
          "end": 53.98,
          "en": "So here we configured this compiler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.98,
          "end": 57.06,
          "en": "and in there you've got various options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.06,
          "end": 59.01,
          "en": "To understand all those options,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 62.96,
          "en": "of course, check out those official docs or my course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.96,
          "end": 64.86,
          "en": "I do dive into greater detail there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.86,
          "end": 68.64,
          "en": "and the official docs also explain all those options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.64,
          "end": 71.05,
          "en": "But you can also hover over an option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.05,
          "end": 74.62,
          "en": "and you will get at least a short description here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.62,
          "end": 77.73,
          "en": "and a link for the more detailed explanation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.73,
          "end": 79.09,
          "en": "so that's very helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.09,
          "end": 80.99,
          "en": "This links to the official docs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.99,
          "end": 83.22,
          "en": "And I'll also walk you through",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.22,
          "end": 85.35,
          "en": "the most important options here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.35,
          "end": 87.213,
          "en": "and that starts with the target.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.13,
          "end": 92.58,
          "en": "This in the end controls the target JavaScript version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.58,
          "end": 95.5,
          "en": "to which your code will be transformed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.5,
          "end": 99.06,
          "en": "And in this case, that's es5 JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.06,
          "end": 101.95,
          "en": "which is quite an old version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.95,
          "end": 104.32,
          "en": "which of course means that you should generally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.32,
          "end": 107.19,
          "en": "have a broad browser support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.19,
          "end": 110.52000000000001,
          "en": "Though I will say, that depending on your project setup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.52000000000001,
          "end": 114.96000000000001,
          "en": "this target option might not be the only thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.96000000000001,
          "end": 117.12,
          "en": "that influences the output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.12,
          "end": 119.66,
          "en": "There also can be project setups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.66,
          "end": 124.38,
          "en": "where your TypeScript code might be compiled to JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 128.49,
          "en": "and then you might have yet another compilation step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.49,
          "end": 131.42,
          "en": "For example, with other tools like Babel,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.42,
          "end": 134.95,
          "en": "that take that output JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.95,
          "end": 137.17000000000002,
          "en": "and transform it even more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.17000000000002,
          "end": 140.55,
          "en": "So that's not necessarily the last step in line",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.55,
          "end": 142.13,
          "en": "but it often will be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.13,
          "end": 143.74,
          "en": "And that then simply controls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.74,
          "end": 146.12,
          "en": "to which kind of JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 146.12,
          "end": 149.46,
          "en": "your TypeScript code is transformed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.46,
          "end": 154.1,
          "en": "Now here we see some default TypeScript libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.1,
          "end": 158.99,
          "en": "that are included and that influences which kind of types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.99,
          "end": 162.92000000000002,
          "en": "are known out of the box by our TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.92000000000002,
          "end": 166.61,
          "en": "And these are some libraries which are actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.61,
          "end": 168.56,
          "en": "built into TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.56,
          "end": 171.688,
          "en": "so we don't need to install some extra packages here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.688,
          "end": 175.05,
          "en": "but to unlock them in this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.05,
          "end": 177.203,
          "en": "we still need to list them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.09,
          "end": 181.63,
          "en": "Now the DOM lib which is added here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.63,
          "end": 184.48,
          "en": "ensures that some default DOM types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.48,
          "end": 186.95,
          "en": "are understood by TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.95,
          "end": 189.72,
          "en": "And a great example here can be found",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.72,
          "end": 192.02,
          "en": "in the NewTodo.tsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.02,
          "end": 195.27,
          "en": "This HTMLInputElement type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.27,
          "end": 198.28,
          "en": "I mentioned that this is a built-in type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.28,
          "end": 201.81,
          "en": "and it's actually such a built-in type that it's unlocked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.81,
          "end": 205.883,
          "en": "because we have that DOM lib added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.73,
          "end": 211.21,
          "en": "If I would remove DOM here from lib and save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.21,
          "end": 213.13,
          "en": "then eventually here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.13,
          "end": 215.43,
          "en": "you see I'm getting an error down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 215.43,
          "end": 217.68,
          "en": "That value does not exist on this type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 217.68,
          "end": 221.82999999999998,
          "en": "because it actually doesn't fully understand this type then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.82999999999998,
          "end": 226.63,
          "en": "So that's an important lib which we should have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.63,
          "end": 229.69299999999998,
          "en": "So in here I'll bring back DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.48,
          "end": 235.28,
          "en": "Now for those other settings, allowJs controls that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 235.28,
          "end": 239.01,
          "en": "we could also include just .JS files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.01,
          "end": 242.7,
          "en": "so plain JavaScript files in our projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.7,
          "end": 245.88,
          "en": "And import from such a plain JavaScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.88,
          "end": 247.39,
          "en": "without causing an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 247.39,
          "end": 251.69,
          "en": "if we wanna mix and match TypeScript and JavaScript files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.69,
          "end": 253.913,
          "en": "that's possible with this option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 254.8,
          "end": 256.24,
          "en": "Then we got a couple of options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.24,
          "end": 258.84,
          "en": "which are not that important for us here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 258.84,
          "end": 261.63,
          "en": "Very important though, is the strict option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 261.63,
          "end": 263.51,
          "en": "This is set to true which means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 263.51,
          "end": 266.55,
          "en": "that we have the strictest possible settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.55,
          "end": 268.04,
          "en": "for this project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 268.04,
          "end": 269.49,
          "en": "And that for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 269.49,
          "end": 274.49,
          "en": "influences that we can't have implicitly any values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 274.99,
          "end": 278.38,
          "en": "as we had it with parameters in the past.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.38,
          "end": 281.81,
          "en": "If we had a parameter somewhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 281.81,
          "end": 283.81,
          "en": "where we didn't set the type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 283.81,
          "end": 286.03,
          "en": "for example, if I remove the type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 286.03,
          "end": 289.46,
          "en": "then we get those squiggly lines that it implicitly has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 289.46,
          "end": 293.32,
          "en": "the any type and with strict mode, that's not allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 293.32,
          "end": 297.25,
          "en": "We have to explicitly set a type in places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 297.25,
          "end": 300.68,
          "en": "where TypeScript is not able to infer it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 300.68,
          "end": 305.47,
          "en": "Strict true also unlocks a couple of other strict features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 305.47,
          "end": 308.43,
          "en": "but this non-implicit any type feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 308.43,
          "end": 312,
          "en": "is the most important one for us here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 312,
          "end": 313.1,
          "en": "Then we've got more options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 313.1,
          "end": 315.76,
          "en": "which are not that important for us here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 315.76,
          "end": 318.1,
          "en": "The jsx option is interesting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 318.1,
          "end": 321.86,
          "en": "It basically controls that jsx code is supported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 321.86,
          "end": 324.91,
          "en": "and which output code should be generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 324.91,
          "end": 328.13,
          "en": "And in general, the default settings which we got here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 328.13,
          "end": 329.68,
          "en": "of course should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 329.68,
          "end": 331.14,
          "en": "And you should only change them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 331.14,
          "end": 333.18,
          "en": "if you know what you're doing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 333.18,
          "end": 336.38,
          "en": "But you can configure your TypeScripts behavior here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 336.38,
          "end": 338.3,
          "en": "and you now have a rough understanding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 338.3,
          "end": 339.73,
          "en": "of what this file does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 339.73,
          "end": 342.26,
          "en": "Again you can always dive into the official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 342.26,
          "end": 344.733,
          "en": "to learn more about those different settings.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}